     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"The crown is reachable through two independent routes. Route A: edge2 -> h1_1:escalate -> h2_0:access -> h4_0:access or h4_3:access. Route B: h1_2:pivot -> h3_1:escalate -> h4_2:reach. These routes share no blockable step, so blocking one step cannot stop both, and at least 2 blocks are needed. Blocking h1_1:escalate cuts h2_0, h2_1 and h3_2, which removes h4_0, h4_3 and the h3_2 path into h4_2. Blocking h1_2:pivot cuts h3_1 and h2_3, which removes the other paths into h4_2. With both blocked, every parent of crown:obtain is unreachable, so the minimum is 2.\"}"
